<title>GERMANY: West German April industry orders rise 3.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German April industry orders rise 3.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Apr 97     Mar 97	Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +3.3	 +0.6	  +2.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+5.3	 +4.7	  +0.9</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		101.0	 97.8	  95.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data. The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   Apr 97   Mar 97   Apr 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders		+3.1     +0.6	89.8</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 +3.6     +0.8     123.2</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +1.5     +0.9     102.3</p>
<p> Capital goods		  +4.5     +0.4     102.9</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   +5.9     +0.1	94.4</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Jan/Feb 97:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +2.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Mar/Apr 97 with Mar/Apr 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +4.8</p>
<p> Domestic orders			+1.1</p>
<p> Foreign orders			+10.4</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +8.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +0.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +3.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
